.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-config-rollback 1  "rev-stealth-config-rollback " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-config\-rollback \- P6.4: Restore a previously captured `.bak.<epoch>` backup onto the target\*(Aqs current path. The current file (if any) is preserved as a fresh `.bak.<epoch>` by routing the restore write through `ConfigWriter::write_with_backup`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth config rollback\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-target\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIBAK_NAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Restore a previously captured .bak.<epoch> backup onto the target\*(Aqs current path. The current file (if any) is preserved as a fresh .bak.<epoch> via ConfigWriter::write_with_backup. Path traversal is rejected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: side\-effect\-free plan emission. No file writes, no network calls, no keyring operations. Returns exit 0 after emitting the structured plan envelope
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: include the action plan in the result envelope\*(Aqs `result.plan` field. Can be combined with `\-\-dry\-run`. When passed without `\-\-dry\-run`, the plan is emitted alongside the real action
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fI<IDEMPOTENCY_KEY>\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5 / G.6: opaque caller\-supplied key for at\-most\-once commit semantics. Accepted in G.5; surfaced in the envelope; the underlying commit replay semantics land in G.6
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR [default: policy]
Which file to roll back. Defaults to `policy`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
policy
.IP \(bu 2
authorized
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIBAK_NAME\fR>
The exact backup filename to restore (e.g. `policy.toml.bak.1700000000000`). Resolved relative to the target file\*(Aqs parent directory. Path traversal is rejected
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth config rollback policy.toml.bak.1700000000000
  $ rev\-stealth config rollback authorized.toml.bak.1700000000000 \-\-target authorized

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Rollback committed.
  1  UserError        Bad backup name / path traversal / not found.
  3  PermanentError   ConfigWriter IO failure.

ENV:
  REV_SCRAPING_POLICY      Override the policy.toml path.
  REV_SCRAPING_AUTHORIZED  Override the authorized.toml path.
